"title": "Synthetic Variables \u2013 Increased Latency",
"updated_at": "2026-01-27T22:26:08.018Z",
"url": "https://stspg.io/jwf9809pr9l4"
},
{
"body": "Summary:\n We identified an issue that limited the number of active connections to one of our servers. The root cause was a kernel-level restriction on the maximum number of open files (file descriptors), which also affects network sockets.\nImpact:\n The limitation caused a temporary reduction in the number of simultaneous connections the server could handle, potentially affecting availability for some users.\nResolution:\n The kernel and system-level limits for open files were increased to ensure sufficient capacity for concurrent connections. After applying the changes and restarting the affected services, the system returned to normal operation.\nPreventive Actions:\n We\u2019ve updated our configuration management to enforce higher default limits across all environments, preventing similar constraints in the future.\nStatus:\nThis incident has been fully resolved, and all systems are operating normally.",
"first_seen": "2026-09-04T07:06:16Z",
"impact": "critical",
"last_seen": "2026-09-09T12:30:34Z",
"resolved_at": "2025-11-01T15:12:33.504Z",
"resolved_inferred": false,
"started_at": "2025-10-31T13:28:39.672Z",
"state": "resolved",
"title": "[UbiFunction] Module experiencing degradation",
"updated_at": "2025-11-01T15:12:33.526Z",
"url": "https://stspg.io/82g1805cwkm0"
},
